Third-party software in the Pepper worker image (Dockerfile.worker)
===================================================================

The worker image redistributes the following tools unmodified. Each runs as a
separate program (invoked as a child process); none is linked into Pepper.
Versions and SHA-256 checksums are pinned in Dockerfile.worker.

OpenGrep 1.30.0 (rule-based SAST)
  https://github.com/opengrep/opengrep
  License: LGPL-2.1

Trivy 0.72.0 (container / IaC scanning)
  https://github.com/aquasecurity/trivy
  License: Apache-2.0

jadx 1.5.6 (Android APK / AAB / DEX decompiler; compiled-code scan)
  https://github.com/skylot/jadx
  Copyright 2013-present skylot and jadx contributors
  License: Apache-2.0 (full text in the image at /opt/jadx/LICENSE)
  The jadx distribution bundles third-party libraries under their own
  licenses (Apache-2.0, BSD, MIT, EPL); see the jadx project for details.

Vineflower 1.12.0 (Java bytecode decompiler; compiled-code scan)
  https://github.com/Vineflower/vineflower
  Copyright the Vineflower and Fernflower (JetBrains) contributors
  License: Apache-2.0 (https://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0)

ILSpy command-line decompiler, ilspycmd 11.1.0.9782 (.NET decompiler;
compiled-code scan), with ICSharpCode.Decompiler and its dependencies
  https://github.com/icsharpcode/ILSpy
  Copyright (c) 2011-2026 AlphaSierraPapa for the SharpDevelop Team
  License: MIT (text below). Bundled dependencies (McMaster.Extensions.*,
  Microsoft.Extensions.*, K4os.Compression.LZ4, NuGet libraries) are MIT or
  Apache-2.0 licensed.

.NET Runtime 10.0.12 (runs ilspycmd)
  https://github.com/dotnet/runtime
  Copyright (c) .NET Foundation and Contributors
  License: MIT. License and third-party notices in the image at
  /usr/share/dotnet/LICENSE.txt and /usr/share/dotnet/ThirdPartyNotices.txt.

OpenJDK 21 (Alpine package openjdk21-jre-headless; runs jadx and Vineflower)
  https://openjdk.org
  License: GNU General Public License, version 2, with the Classpath
  Exception. License and notices in the image under
  /usr/lib/jvm/java-21-openjdk/legal/. Source code is available from the
  OpenJDK project and the Alpine Linux aports repository.

Apache-2.0: https://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0
LGPL-2.1:   https://www.gnu.org/licenses/old-licenses/lgpl-2.1.html
GPLv2 + Classpath Exception: https://openjdk.org/legal/gplv2+ce.html

